<article class="env-lemma" id="098J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/098J">Lemma <span data-tag="098J">61.31.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathit{Sch}_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}$ be a big pro-étale site as in Definition <a href="/tag/098G" data-tag="098G">61.12.7</a>. Let $T \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathit{Sch}_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale})$. Let $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ be an arbitrary pro-étale covering of $T$. There exists a covering $\{ U_ j \to T\} _{j \in J}$ of $T$ in the site $\mathit{Sch}_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}$ which refines $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, we first let $\{ V_ k \to T\} $ be a covering as in Lemma <a href="/tag/098I" data-tag="098I">61.13.3</a>. Then the pro-étale coverings $\{ T_ i \times _ T V_ k \to V_ k\} $ can be refined by a finite disjoint open covering $V_ k = V_{k, 1} \amalg \ldots \amalg V_{k, n_ k}$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/098F" data-tag="098F">61.13.1</a>. Then $\{ V_{k, i} \to T\} $ is a covering of $\mathit{Sch}_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}$ which refines $\{ T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>